## Can foreigners buy here?

Yes. Like everywhere in Mauritius foreigners can buy in Le Morne through the schemes managed by the Economic Development Board: the [PDS](/en/living-in-the-west/pds) and [IRS](/en/living-in-the-west/irs) and [RES](/en/living-in-the-west/res) and [Smart City](/en/living-in-the-west/smart-city) schemes. They can also buy an apartment of at least MUR 6 million in a building with at least two floors above the ground floor. A home of **USD 375 000 or more** comes with a residence permit for as long as you own it.

## What the official lists show

No project on the EDB's November 2022 list of Real Estate Scheme projects is located on the Le Morne peninsula; the nearest are in Black River and Tamarin. There is no smart city on the peninsula; the nearest is Cap Tamarin. The RES list dates from 2022 and the EDB does not publish a full list of PDS projects on its website so ask any developer for its current scheme certificate.

## Costs on top of the price

- Registration duty: 5% of the price under the PDS. Under the IRS and RES it is USD 70 000 or 5% on a first purchase (whichever is lower).
- The EDB's processing fee: MUR 25 000 per application.
- Notary fees: ask for a written quote.

The full process from reservation to residence permit is in [how buying works](/en/living-in-the-west/how-buying-works).

## Living in Le Morne

Port Louis is about 48 km away by car (roughly 53 minutes with no traffic). Schools and clinics and costs and daily life are covered in [Living in Le Morne](/en/areas/le-morne#living).

*Figures come from the official sources listed below and were checked on 3 October 2026. Prices change so ask local agents and schools and your notary for current figures before you decide.*
